      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you've suffered a second-degree burn. Applying a thick layer of lubricating ointment, such as aloe vera or petroleum jelly, can help protect the burned area and promote healing. However, butter is not the best option, as it can slow healing and trap bacteria. If the pain is intense, you may also want to consider applying an over-the-counter pain reliever like acetaminophen or ibuprofen once the wound is properly cleaned.",
